Revision history for Mojo::Centrifuge

0.30  2026-11-01
    - Epoch + recover semantics: subscribe accepts {recover, epoch,
      offset} and returns {epoch, recovered, offset, publications?}
    - Publications carry optional tags; wire, history, and recover
      replay all preserve them
    - connect result returns real token expires (epoch seconds, 0 =
      never); expired tokens close the session with error 109
    - client_channel_limit (default 128) per connection, per namespace
    - namespaces attribute: per-family history_size, history_ttl,
      presence, presence_ttl, presence_events, client_channel_limit,
      force_recover, epoch_key_ttl
    - Reserved channel prefixes: # (server-only) and $user (private)
    - Rate limits: publish_rate_limit, message_rate_limit
      (per connection, per second, default 0 = unlimited)
    - Server API: POST /api/publish, /api/broadcast, /api/history,
      /api/presence, /api/channels, /api/unsubscribe, /api/disconnect,
      /api/info, /api/history_remove, /api/revoke; GET /api/status
    - Prometheus /metrics endpoint
    - New methods: channel_info, history_remove, revoke_user,
      channel_stats
    - Routes extracted to Mojo::Centrifuge::ExampleApp so example.pl
      and t/basic.t share one definition
    - Legacy /publish is POST + JSON only
    - Fix: _namespace_of('room1') returned 'room1' instead of ''
    - Fix: connect.expires hardcoded to 1
    - Tests: t/08-epoch.t, t/09-expiry.t, t/10-namespaces.t,
      t/11-rate.t added; t/basic.t is now a real API integration test

0.21  2026-10-31
        - Phase 2: wired Mojo::Centrifuge::Protocol into the WebSocket
          handler. `protocol => 'centrifuge'` now speaks the Centrifugo
          JSON protocol (connect/subscribe/unsubscribe/publish/presence/
          refresh/ping, result/error/push frames). Default remains
          'legacy'.
        - New attribute history_ttl (seconds, 0 = no expiry). When > 0,
          the history key gets refreshed on every publish.
        - New attribute presence_ttl (seconds, default 60). Presence is
          now a Redis ZSET scored by join time; stale entries are
          lazily removed on presence() queries.
        - Legacy error replies are now structured: {error: {code,
          message}} instead of a bare string. Message text is unchanged,
          so clients matching on text keep working; clients matching on
          the raw {error} value must use {error}{message}.
        - Mojo::Centrifuge::Protocol now exports the ERR_* codes via
          Exporter (:codes tag or individually).
        - Added t/05-presence-ttl.t, t/06-centrifuge-wire.t,
          t/07-history-ttl.t (mock Redis, no external services).
        - ws_client.pl: two error-regex assertions updated to inspect
          {error}{message} instead of the bare {error} string.

0.20  2026-10-31
        - Phase 1: added Mojo::Centrifuge::Protocol (Centrifugo JSON
          frame codec, not yet wired into the WS handler).
        - Auth: switched signature comparison to Mojo::Util::secure_compare.
        - Added POD to all public subs; pass AUTHOR_TESTING=1 with
          Test::Pod and Test::Pod::Coverage.
        - example.pl and make_token.pl are repo examples only, not
          installed by Makefile.PL.
        - Bumped $VERSION in Mojo::Centrifuge, Mojo::Centrifuge::Auth,
          and added $VERSION to Mojo::Centrifuge::Protocol.

0.19  2026-10-31
        - Baseline: HMAC tokens, WS subscribe/unsubscribe, Redis
          history + since replay, presence, keepalive, server API key,
          client publish with permission check, glob authorization.
